    "result_text": "I added a **Send all drafts** button to the selected client's invoice list. `bin/e2e` passes, including the replay of earlier test data.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Server:** a new endpoint, `POST /api/clients/{clientId}/invoices/send-drafts`, calls `InvoiceService.sendAllDrafts`. That goes through the client's drafts lowest id first and sends each one that has at least one line. Drafts with no lines stay drafts, and other clients' invoices aren't touched.\n- **Same as sending by hand:** I moved the sending step out of `send()` into a shared helper, `markSent`, which both paths now use. Bulk sends therefore get exactly the same dates (issued today, or the test's `asOf` date, and due on the client's terms) and the same `INVOICE_SENT` audit line.\n- **All or nothing:** everything runs in one transaction, so if any send fails, none of them are kept.\n- **Front end:** the button (`invoice-send-all`) is next to \"New invoice\". After a send, the list updates with the new statuses and dates, and the client's balance refreshes.\n- **Open invoice panel:** if an invoice was open when you clicked the button, its panel now reloads so it shows as sent. To do this I added a small `reload` input to `invoice-panel.ts`.\n\nThe button is clickable even when the client has no drafts with lines; it just does nothing then.",
